  "investigation_notes": "Uploads are failing because `incidentlab-app-1` cannot reach `incidentlab-db-1`.\n\nRoot cause - database detached from network:\n- `incidentlab-app-1` is on `[\"incidentlab_default\"]` (E5) while `incidentlab-db-1` is on `[]` - no networks (E6).\n- Both containers were recreated/restarted at `00:01:47-00:01:53` (E4). `app` `Up 5 seconds`, `db` `Up 11 seconds (healthy)` (E1). `db` `started_at 00:01:47`, `app` `started_at 00:01:53` (E5, E6).\n- This explains DNS failure, not a database crash.\n\nSymptoms in app, caused by dependency:\n- App `/health` is `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n- App logs show `upload` at `/app/main.py line 65` and `health` at `line 113` both failing with `psycopg.OperationalError: failed to resolve host 'db': [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution` (E3).\n- Database itself is healthy: `health: healthy` (E6), `pg_isready` execs succeeded and `health_status: healthy` (E4), logs show `database system is ready to accept connections` with no errors, listening on `5432` (E7).\n\nStorage ruled out for uploads path `/srv/lab-data/uploads`:\n- Filesystem holding `/srv/lab-data` is `9.0%` used, `410.6 MB` available, `inode 0.2%` (E8) - not full.\n- `/srv/lab-data/uploads` is dir `0755` owned `1000:1000` (E9), `/srv/lab-data` same (E10), app runs as `1000:1000` (E5) with `app_user_can_write: true` (E9, E10).\n- Bind mount present: `/srv/lab-data -> /data rw:true` (E5).\n\nConclusion: application unhealthy due to loss of network connectivity to healthy database, not disk or permissions.\n",
